Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["FormWedge", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"de64be1e-421f-43d7-974d-7fd0cd338631"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["FormWedge"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FormWedge", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TR"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TR"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55ff967e-fdc6-4efa-a4f7-dadc956bb78e"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the wedge product ",
 StyleBox["\[Omega] \[And] \[Eta]", "TI"],
 " of the forms ",
 StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"],
 ", the exterior product of their germs at every vertex.",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"7747c4c4-d7c4-4853-aeba-73fcbde9bb3f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 "-form ",
 StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"],
 " and a ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 "-form ",
 StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"],
 ", with ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " = ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " + ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["(\[Omega] \[And] \[Eta])(v; w\:2081, \[Ellipsis], w\:2099)", 
  "TI"],
 " is the sum of ",
 StyleBox["sgn(\[Sigma]) \[Omega](v; w\[Sigma]\:208d\:2081\:208e, \
\[Ellipsis], w\[Sigma]\:208d\:209a\:208e) \[Eta](v; w\[Sigma]\:208d\:209a\
\:208a\:2081\:208e, \[Ellipsis], w\[Sigma]\:208d\:2099\:208e)", "TI"],
 " over the shuffles ",
 StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"],
 ", the permutations that keep the first ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " and the last ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 " places in order. For two 1-forms, ",
 StyleBox["(\[Omega] \[And] \[Eta])(v; w\:2081, w\:2082) = \[Omega](v; \
w\:2081) \[Eta](v; w\:2082) \[Minus] \[Omega](v; w\:2082) \[Eta](v; w\:2081)",
   "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3076a6de-af4d-4261-90b8-ff6f2ec80448"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On 0-forms it is the product of functions, and a 0-form times a ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 "-form multiplies the germ at each vertex by the value there."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"cd5ef9eb-bad5-4328-a198-7825feb0fedc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The product is associative and graded-commutative, ",
 StyleBox["\[Eta] \[And] \[Omega] = \[Omega] \[And] \[Eta]", "TI"],
 " with a minus sign when ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 " are both odd. So ",
 StyleBox["\[Omega] \[And] \[Omega] = 0", "TI"],
 " for a 1-form."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"623de010-fabe-4403-b0a8-fa667d410f61"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The differential is not a derivation for it: on 0-forms ",
 StyleBox["d(f \[And] h) \[Minus] df \[And] h \[Minus] f \[And] dh", "TI"],
 " is the step-by-step product ",
 StyleBox["(f(w) \[Minus] f(v))(h(w) \[Minus] h(v))", "TI"],
 " of the gradients."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3954ab3f-add0-47e8-bddb-3bd43ea7c6e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On the square grid ",
 StyleBox["(dx \[And] dy)(v; w\:2081, w\:2082)", "TI"],
 " is the determinant of the steps ",
 StyleBox["w\:2081 \[Minus] v", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["w\:2082 \[Minus] v", "TI"],
 ", \[PlusMinus]1 or 0. The grid has no triangles, so the integral of every \
2-form is 0. On the square mesh the integral of ",
 StyleBox["dx \[And] dy", "TI"],
 " is ",
 StyleBox["2 \[Delta]x \:222a \[Delta]y", "TI"],
 " (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["CochainCup"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/CochainCup", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "56b7cec6-add5-4622-b9d9-f384f8092c66"],
 "), twice the signed area of each triangle."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c061d9fb-5c9e-4700-8178-c728967a05be"],

Cell["\<\
The product has a germ at the vertices where both factors have one.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d9ef1b38-c1a4-4243-a202-cd8c51d4b9b6"]
}, Open  ]],

